#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0095 expect=noViolation domain=SUPPSV
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner, queued item C3, as c5206c02): RDOMAIN names a domain, and dataset names match case-insensitively (owner 2026-10-01), so the literal comparison reads upper(RDOMAIN). Copy of PMDA-SD0095-valid_sv_exempt-SUPPSV.cdt with the RDOMAIN cells lower-cased; the expected outcome is the original one. Red under the old exact comparison."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
#library dataset-class SV "SPECIAL PURPOSE"
dataset SUPPSV class=RELATIONSHIP label="Supplemental Qualifiers for SV"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col QNAM    type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL    type=Char label="Data Value"
---
S1 | sv | 001 | VISITREA | Unscheduled visit reason
